{"h":3396,"lines":[{"x":0.83283537917467432,"y":0.031364378658118475,"w":0.085508651733398389,"h":0.019818210489477517,"t":"Reading","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.078189298397513193,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"Questions 17-20","y":0.081272084871531924,"w":0.17901234944661459},{"t":"Complete the summary using the list of words, A-H, below.","c":1,"x":0.07818929088398803,"y":0.11773255852767572,"w":0.56172841389973949,"h":0.018898772968701127},{"c":1,"h":0.018979236571331048,"x":0.078189287750305148,"t":"Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 17-20 on your answer sheet.","w":0.63786010742187504,"y":0.15253239094070237},{"h":0.02041046919895706,"w":0.55761316935221361,"c":1,"y":0.18895348817510049,"t":"We should be more tolerant of microbes","x":0.22016460886956082},{"y":0.23386069327769443,"c":1,"w":0.74701370239257814,"t":"Yong's book argues that we should be more tolerant of microbes. Many have a","x":0.076078756776979992,"h":0.019395433971822862},{"c":1,"w":0.59889790852864588,"x":0.076056740356207131,"h":0.019470239556158675,"t":"beneficial effect, and only a relatively small number lead to 17 ...","y":0.25797930130415936},{"t":"... And","x":0.82304526619594109,"y":0.25872093004680674,"w":0.063786010742187482,"c":1,"h":0.016014052504504606},{"h":0.017493220465202852,"t":"although it is misleading to think of microbes as 'friendly', we should also stop thinking of","x":0.076131694448603848,"y":0.28197674402534412,"c":1,"w":0.84156377156575535},{"c":1,"w":0.82304524739583318,"t":"them as the enemy. In fact, we should accept that our relationship with microbes is one","y":0.30523255797781323,"x":0.076131697295616529,"h":0.017500068610632802},{"c":1,"w":0.13580247243245441,"t":"based on 18 ...","x":0.076131685478957253,"y":0.32979976453354354,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"c":1,"x":0.078189292297820623,"t":"New research shows that microbes have numerous benefits for humans. Amongst other","y":0.36918604634922669,"h":0.017445284570484998,"w":0.83127573649088538},{"t":"things, th